{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted sourced research feedback recording one more lead before the run's budget expires, with three new SourceRanges (S-future-defer, future.go:92-122; S-api-shutdown, api.go:1012-1025; S-raft-run-exit, raft.go:135-157). The mechanism: a client future created by Apply/ApplyLog does not receive the node's shutdown channel, because deferError.Error() selects only on the response channel or d.ShutdownCh and init() creates only the response channel, while the three places that set ShutdownCh are the user-restore future, the snapshot-install future and the snapshot request. The main run loop exits when shutdownCh closes without draining applyCh, and Shutdown closes shutdownCh and sets the state without answering futures already enqueued, so with Config.BatchApplyCh buffering the channel a future can be accepted while the loop is busy and then be abandoned at shutdown, leaving the caller blocked indefinitely instead of receiving ErrRaftShutdown. The discriminating experiment is recorded (enable BatchApplyCh, enqueue an Apply while the loop is occupied, shut down, observe whether the future ever resolves), along with the open questions of reachability and intended behaviour. No map change is proposed because A7's unknown already states that the future timeout semantics were not fully traced and this narrows it rather than contradicting it. Run state at submission: six confirmed_in_scope conclusions across eight implementation_reproduced findings, a fully mapped surface set plus the one deferred Restore-reporting surface, and about 765 seconds of budget remaining. Preflight returned valid:true.\"}"}}
